Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: switch the SFP cages' line rate at runtime

The Gateway DK's two cages sit on MAC9 and MAC10, pinned at 10GBASE-R by a
fixed-link. With the cage attached to the netdev (the previous patch) a 1G
or 2.5G module is detected, but nothing on the host side can talk to it: a
GPON stick, a 1000BASE-X optic or a copper SFP never gets a link.

Pick a line rate from what the module offers (sfp_parse_support() and the
sfp quirks) and move the hardware to it at runtime, fastest first, keeping
the first mode whose PCS reports link: 10GBASE-R, 2500BASE-X, 1000BASE-X
with and without clause 37 negotiation, SGMII. "ethtool -s ethX speed N
autoneg off" pins a rate; "autoneg on" returns to the search.

A switch moves:
 - the SerDes1 lane: protocol, equalisation, PLL and rate, with the values
   of mainline phy-fsl-lynx-10g.c, and the RCW override of mainline
   soc/fsl/guts.c that swaps the lane between the MAC's XGMII and GMII
   sides. 1G runs from PLL1, the 100 MHz-referenced PLL of the copper SGMII
   ports. 2500BASE-X needs 3.125 GHz, which only PLL2 (156.25 MHz, the XFI
   PLL) can make: PLL1 hangs the SoC when reset at 3.125 GHz, while a reset
   at 5 GHz relocks at once. So one cage at 2.5G and the other at 10G cannot
   coexist on this board; both at 2.5G, or any mix of 10G and 1G, can.
 - the DS100DF410 retimer channels in front of the cage: CDR at 10G, raw
   mode below (TI SNLA323), as their CDR only locks at 10.3125G.
 - the mEMAC and its PCS, through a new FM_MAC_SetEnetMode().

PLL2 goes to 10G when both want it: a cage at 2.5G gives way (falls back
to 1G) while the other cage is open with a 10G-capable module, whichever
came up first. An ethtool-forced 2.5G keeps the PLL.

The link a port reports becomes LOS and the 10GBASE-R PCS together at 10G
(a DAC has no LOS), the 1G PCS alone below: a stick stays reachable over
its host link without fibre. An up link has to read down three times,
100 ms apart, before the carrier drops, and a failed PCS read keeps the
last state: single bad reads (seen every few minutes on a 1000BASE-X
MA5671A link) otherwise cost a bridge port its STP listening/learning time.

Fix a NULL dereference in memac_sfp_link_update() from the previous patch:
the fixed-PHY link_update callback stays registered across a stop/start,
and on the next start of_phy_connect() re-probes the fixed PHY before
attached_dev is set, so "ip link set ethX up" after a down oopsed with
rtnl held (seen as a watchdog reboot).

Also give slow GPON sticks three minutes to answer on the EEPROM bus
instead of one: a Huawei MA5671A was still booting when the cage gave up.

Lanes, PLLs and retimer channels were measured on a DK. Tested there with
a Ubiquiti DAC-SFP10-1M to a MikroTik CRS309 (10G, and 2.5G with the
switch port forced) and a Huawei MA5671A (1000BASE-X and 2500BASE-X),
including runtime 2.5G <-> 1G switches with the PLL retune and cage
down/up cycles.
